## [ISSUE] Hidden attributes are only hidden while the user is searching

**Severity:** MEDIUM — HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES is only applied inside the search-filter branch; when the search box is empty (the default) the early `return sorted` still shows is_segment/project_id/received.

### The Problem
```tsx
const sorted = sortAttributes(attributes);
if (!searchQuery.trim()) {
  return sorted;              // HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES not applied
}
return sorted.filter(attribute => !HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES.includes(attribute.name) && ...);
```

### Theory / Proof
The hide filter only runs in the non-empty-search branch, so the default render path skips it.

### What happens today vs. what will break
On first open of the span drawer, `is_segment`, `project_id` and `received` are still listed. They only disappear once the user types a query. Typing and then clearing the query makes them reappear, which looks like flicker.

### Research
N/A. Straightforward control-flow issue.

### Recommendation
```tsx
const sorted = sortAttributes(attributes).filter(a => !HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES.includes(a.name));
if (!searchQuery.trim()) {
  return sorted;
}
return sorted.filter(a => a.name.toLowerCase().trim().includes(searchQuery.toLowerCase().trim()));
```
